 "claim": "Three-fold spaces are an Euler count. Resolution refutations compose over the handle tree at constant cost per Fano piece (Davis-Putnam derivations of the pieces' port relations, width at most 5), so every three-fold space costs at most its core plus O(number of pieces). On a plane core with Kasteleyn signs the contradiction is Euler's count: a satisfied line has exactly one agreeing corner, every face at least one, and there are two more faces than lines; assignments modulo complement are exactly the parity solutions on the line-face graph, and not-all-equal asks degree one at every line. Hence Sherali-Adams of level max(3, d) refutes every plane signed space whose faces carry at most d points (level 3 on the octahedral family) and constant level refutes its decorations, while resolution gets the treewidth bound n^O(1) 2^O(sqrt n) for every three-fold space. On the octahedral family, a single brace for every k, solver costs grow by factors of 7 to 50 per step in k; a resolution lower bound 2^Omega(sqrt n) is conjectured, not proved.",
 "kind": "proof",
